# VVDN — 3 synthetic aircraft in trail from DOTEN, 3-minute spacing, Trombone
# vectoring into ILS V 35L (RWY 35L), landing, then 2 different ground exits.
# Built 2026-08 per user spec; callsigns VDN601/602/603 are SYNTHETIC (not
# real ADS-B flights, unlike VVDN_HVN337_ARR_EVA384_DEP_REAL.scn) — flagged
# clearly so this is never mistaken for real traffic data.
#
# REAL DATA USED (sources):
#  - DOTEN 15.767222,108.118333 -> TRACO 15.601667,108.142222 -> CADAS
#    15.618056,108.262500 -> MONRY 15.700556,108.250000 -> TAMLA
#    15.788333,108.237500 -> KALET 15.873556,108.223089 -> FAF35
#    15.957231,108.210955 — the REAL published route (corrected after an
#    earlier wrong first attempt routed DOTEN via TAWAN, a different real
#    entry transition that does NOT touch DOTEN). Confirmed from
#    WebATM/static/data/vatm_kmz/procedures_by_airport/vatm_procedures_VVDN.geojson:
#    STAR RWY 35's real named legs DOTEN-TRACO / TRACO-CADAS / CADAS-MONRY /
#    MONRY-TAMLA, then TAMLA feeds into ILS V 35L's own "Initial TAML"
#    transition (TAMLA-KALET) through to the shared Intermediate/Final legs.
#  - RWY 35L threshold 16.030125,108.200392 hdg352, and the 3NM/1NM/short-
#    final/touchdown points (15.980645,108.207626 / 16.013632,108.202804 /
#    16.029556,108.200443 / 16.036501,108.199490) — reused verbatim from
#    VVDN_HVN337_ARR_EVA384_DEP_REAL.scn, itself a real-ADS-B-anchored
#    reconstruction of the same RWY35L final approach.
#  - Real RWY 35L (17R/35L) far end 16.057080,108.196439 and taxiway G4
#    (16.048721,108.197655 -> 16.049646,108.199646) / G6 (16.057080,108.196439
#    -> 16.057400,108.198412) — FTS Server/data/aerodrome_layout/datasets/
#    vietnam_kml_layout/normalized/airports/VVDN/taxiway_centerlines.geojson.
#    G4's start point matches HVN337's real turn-off (16.048622,108.197792,
#    ~11m away) — confirms it's the same real taxiway the user referenced.
#  - Real Gate 11 16.057808,108.201333 — same dataset's gates.geojson
#    (0.5m from the user-supplied 16.0578,108.2013).
#  - REAL crossing altitudes (v3), from the official AIP Vietnam STAR chart
#    "STANDARD ARRIVAL CHART - INSTRUMENT (STAR) - ICAO, DA NANG/DA NANG INTL
#    (VVDN), RNAV RWY 35L/R" (AD 2-VVDN-11-7/8/11, AIRAC AMDT 01/23), tabular
#    description common to all 9 published transitions (HUE/CAHEO/BUNTA/CQ/
#    KUMUN/SADIN/VILOT/LATOM/PAPRA 2K) that converge through DOTEN-TRACO-
#    CADAS-MONRY-TAMLA identically: MONRY +1500m=4921ft (real published max
#    speed 390km/h=210kt, applied here); TAMLA +1350m=4429ft (user-confirmed).
#    KALET 790m=2592ft and FAF35 450m=1476ft are from the ILS V RWY35L IAP
#    chart's own DME DAD table (D9.6/D4.6 DAD).
#  - DOTEN altitude v3 (11000ft = FL110, replacing the earlier 6070ft): the
#    published chart's "+1850m/6070ft" at DOTEN is only the minimum crossing
#    restriction, not the altitude arrivals actually fly it at -- per user
#    feedback (real ATC operational knowledge), aircraft typically still cross
#    DOTEN around FL110 and get stepped down further along the STAR. TRACO and
#    CADAS carry NO published altitude on the real chart ("–" in both
#    columns), so both were recomputed (8200ft / 6300ft, was 5500ft/5100ft in
#    v2) by linearly interpolating distance-weighted between the new DOTEN
#    FL110 and the real MONRY 4921ft crossing -- DOTEN-TRACO 10.0NM,
#    TRACO-CADAS 7.0NM, CADAS-MONRY 5.0NM (haversine on the real waypoint
#    coordinates), giving a smooth, constant ~276ft/NM descent gradient the
#    whole way from DOTEN to MONRY (not real charted numbers themselves, but
#    now consistent with both the real endpoints and a realistic descent
#    rate).
#  - NO trombone detour is inserted anywhere in CADAS-MONRY-TAMLA-KALET:
#    corrected per user feedback that this whole stretch must keep holding
#    one continuous course (their real bearings are already within ~1.4 deg
#    of each other -- CADAS-MONRY 351.7, MONRY-TAMLA 352.2, TAMLA-KALET
#    350.8 -- i.e. it's really one long straight final-course-intercept leg,
#    not a place to bend with a lateral detour). An earlier version of this
#    file put a +3NM V-shaped offset between TAMLA and KALET; removed. All 3
#    aircraft fly the identical real route at exact 3-minute CRE spacing,
#    which by itself already maintains the requested in-trail gap -- the
#    "Trombone" the user asked for is represented by this real long,
#    fully-merged final-approach course itself (the classic trombone SHAPE
#    real ATC vectors onto), not a synthetic detour bent into it.
#
# ROLLOUT PHYSICS (VDN601's 60-second full runway vacation): touchdown
# 16.036501,108.199490 to G4's real junction 16.048721,108.197655 is
# 0.7413NM (1372.9m). Solved for constant deceleration from touchdown speed
# 134kt to 15kt (a realistic moderate autobrake, ~2.06 m/s2) reaching 15kt
# at t=29.7s, then a constant 15kt taxi crawl for the remaining 30.3s —
# total exactly 60.0s touchdown-to-fully-clear. VDN601 then continues on
# the SAME real taxiway HVN337 used (per the reference file's own
# turn-off-to-Gate24 data) since the user asked for "like HVN337."
# VDN602/VDN603 instead ride the full 1.248NM touchdown-to-runway-end
# rollout (no early exit), turn right onto real taxiway G6, then straight
# to real Gate 11 — exactly as specified.
#
# SPEED PROFILE (v4) — re-tuned to hold specific IAS bands at specific real
# distances from the RWY 35L threshold (16.030125,108.200392), per explicit
# request: 200-230kt at ~25NM, 160-180kt at ~10NM, 150-160kt at ~5NM.
# Distances computed (haversine) from the threshold to each existing real
# waypoint -- no new waypoints were added, since 3 of them already sit very
# close to the requested distances:
#   TRACO  25.94NM -> 225kt (was 240)   |  both inside the 200-230 band for
#   CADAS  25.00NM -> 215kt (was 230)   |  the ~25NM point (CADAS is almost
#                                         exactly 25.00NM)
#   MONRY  19.99NM -> 210kt (REAL, unchanged -- between the 25NM and 10NM
#                                         bands, already a good gradient step)
#   TAMLA  14.67NM -> 190kt (was 200)   -- interpolation step down toward KALET
#   KALET   9.49NM -> 170kt (was 200)   -- inside the 160-180 band for ~10NM
#   FAF35   4.42NM -> 155kt (was 180)   -- inside the 150-160 band for ~5NM
#     (FAF35 is 4.42NM, not exactly 5.0NM -- closest real charted fix to that
#     distance; flagged honestly rather than adding a synthetic extra point)
# 3NM-final (150.1kt) and everything inside it are unchanged (already real/
# reused from the reference file, and outside the 3 requested bands). This
# gives a smooth, monotonically decreasing IAS schedule from CADAS all the
# way to touchdown: 225-215-210-190-170-155-150.1-140-133 kt.
#
# TAXI-TO-GATE STUCK BUG (found and fixed): VDN601's post-G4 taxi-in path
# (reused verbatim from the real-ADS-B reference file) had one waypoint at
# EXACTLY 0.0kt in the MIDDLE of the route (16.049126,108.200491), not at
# the final gate stop. This is the same underlying engine limitation found
# and fixed in the departure scenarios this session: VNAVSPD never resumes
# acceleration once an aircraft is driven to a true dead stop mid-route --
# VDN601 got permanently stuck there instead of continuing on to Gate 24,
# confirmed live. Fixed by bumping that one waypoint to 4.1kt (matching the
# very next waypoint's speed) -- low enough to preserve the tight-turn
# moment the real data represents, but nonzero so VNAV never has to
# accelerate away from a standstill. VDN602/VDN603's G6->Gate11 taxi has no
# equivalent 0.0kt mid-route waypoint, so they were not affected.
#
# RESOLVED (previously flagged as an open issue here): the apparent altitude
# drop seen in early live telemetry was a units bug in the verification
# scripts (bs.traf.alt is in METERS; scripts read it as feet), not a real
# VNAV/descent problem -- confirmed by cross-checking against POS <acid>.
# A second, real bug WAS found and fixed at the BlueSky engine level: ADDWPT
# was silently dropping alt=0/spd=0 constraints (Python falsy-zero check in
# route.py's addwptStack()), which froze touchdown altitude at ~75ft instead
# of 0. Fixed via an `is not None` check; verified with LISTRTE showing
# touchdown at 0/134 post-fix.

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

# ============ VDN601 — 1st in trail, exits via G4 in 60s (like HVN337) ============
00:00:00.00>CRE VDN601 B738 15.767222 108.118333 172 11000 250.0
00:00:00.00>VDN601 ADDWPT 15.601667,108.142222,8200,225.0
